# Normalize every text file to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout gets CRLF while Linux gets LF, and this
# repo is unusually sensitive to that: doc contract tests pin exact strings
# (some spanning a line break), and tests/chassis-drift.test.mjs hashes the
# +/- payload of a git diff between the two plugins' mirrored lib copies.
# Byte-level guards must not depend on which line ending the checkout used.
#
# This was not theoretical: on 2026-08-07 a pin containing a literal \n
# turned windows-latest CI red while the local gate stayed green, because
# both of its legs read an already-LF working tree and neither could observe
# a fresh CRLF checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
